.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt BIO_FIND_TYPE 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm BIO_find_type ,
.Nm BIO_next ,
.Nm BIO_method_type
.Nd BIO chain traversal
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/bio.h
.Ft BIO *
.Fo BIO_find_type
.Fa "BIO *b"
.Fa "int bio_type"
.Fc
.Ft BIO *
.Fo BIO_next
.Fa "BIO *b"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo BIO_method_type
.Fa "const BIO *b"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn BIO_find_type
searches for a
.Vt BIO
of a given type in a chain, starting at
.Vt BIO
.Fa b .
If
.Em type
is a specific type (such as
.Sy BIO_TYPE_MEM )
then a search is made for a
.Vt BIO
of that type.
If
.Em type
is a general type (such as
.Sy BIO_TYPE_SOURCE_SINK )
then the next matching
.Vt BIO
of the given general type is searched for.
.Fn BIO_find_type
returns the next matching
.Vt BIO
or NULL if none is found.
If
.Em type
is
.Sy BIO_TYPE_NONE
it will not find a match.
.Pp
The following general types are defined:
.Sy BIO_TYPE_DESCRIPTOR ,
.Sy BIO_TYPE_FILTER ,
and
.Sy BIO_TYPE_SOURCE_SINK .
.Pp
For a list of the specific types, see the
.Pa <openssl/bio.h>
header file.
.Pp
.Fn BIO_next
returns the next BIO in a chain.
It can be used to traverse all BIOs in a chain or used in conjunction
with
.Fn BIO_find_type
to find all BIOs of a certain type.
.Pp
.Fn BIO_method_type
returns the type of a BIO.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn BIO_find_type
returns a matching BIO or NULL for no match.
.Pp
.Fn BIO_next
returns the next BIO in a chain.
.Pp
.Fn BIO_method_type
returns the type of the BIO
.Fa b .
.Sh EXAMPLES
Traverse a chain looking for digest BIOs:
.Bd -literal
 BIO *btmp;

 btmp = in_bio; /* in_bio is chain to search through */
 do {
     btmp = BIO_find_type(btmp, BIO_TYPE_MD);
     if (btmp == NULL)
         break; /* Not found */
     /* btmp is a digest BIO, do something with it ...*/
     ...

     btmp = BIO_next(btmp);
 } while (btmp);
.Ed
